#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "Three conventions follow from the international definitions:"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**Parity indices are adjusted.** The ratio of one group to another is folded so it is symmetrical around 1: if the ratio is above 1 it becomes 2 minus its inverse. Publications say which form they use."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**Completion from administrative data is a proxy.** The SDG completion rate is defined over a cohort above the intended age and is measured mainly by household surveys; an EMIS figure is labelled as a proxy."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**Out-of-school counts need every level.** A learner enrolled at any level is in school, so the learner registry must cover all levels or the rate is overstated."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "Worked example: gross enrolment ratio"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "The gross enrolment ratio for a level is total enrolment in that level, regardless of age, as a percentage of the population of official school age for that level."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**Gold stores counts** as at the census reference date: learners enrolled in each level, by area and sex, with levels mapped to ISCED 2011 ([CAP-TRANSFORMATION.5]{1}, [CAP-REFERENCE.4]{2})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**The denominator is reference data:** the population of official school age by area, sex and single year of age, with its source and vintage ([CAP-SEMANTICS.5]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**The semantic layer defines the ratio once,** with its metadata and the edition of the definition it follows ([CAP-SEMANTICS]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**The snapshot is locked** when the census completeness gate reads CLEAR for the area ([CAP-COLLECTION.4]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**Publication applies disclosure control,** then the figure is published with a permanent identifier and its metadata ([CAP-PUBLICATION]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**A revision,** whether a late correction or a new population estimate, is a new version of the snapshot and of the published table; the earlier one stays readable."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "Because the ratio is derived from counts and a versioned denominator, the same definition gives the national figure and every area's figure, and a change of population estimate is visible as a new version rather than a silent shift. The ratio can exceed 100 per cent, which is expected when learners outside the official age are enrolled."
msgstr ""
